Demo_1.4_SQLite_Read_from_db_Multiple_Steps
======================================
Requirement: 
	1. From MYSQL Database Pump the Data of Employees  to a (output_db.xml) XML file.
	2. From employee.csv Pump the Data of Employees  to a (output.xml) XML file.
	use SQLite as Job Repo /MetaData Database
Note: first pump Database data to XML and then Later CSV  file Data to Database
	
Pre-requisite:
	Execute Employee.sql file script in MySQL database.
	
Observations:
 1) Open pom.xml file and observe the dependencies
 2) spring-config.xml for meta data configuration in resources folder
 		Highlight usage of SQLLite Database----IMP
 3) spring-batch-config.xml for reader/processor and Writer
 		Highlight Database Reader-------IMP
 		Highlight FlatFile Reader-------IMP
 	(reader can be Flat file, XML, JMS Reader, DAtabse Reader/Customer Reader)
 	(writer can  be Flat file, XML, JMS, Database/Custom Writer)
 	(Tell about Job->Step->Tasklet->Chunk->ItemReader and ItemWriter)
 	(commit interval means how many records can be read in a single chunk we will see it later..)
 	
 	Highlight how a job can have 2 steps using next.
 	Each Step has its on reader and Writer
 			Linking Step to Next one.
				<batch:step id="step1" next="step2">
 4)Open UITester, highlight a job can have multiple instances.
 	Instance actual run the Job.
 	instances are uniquely identified by JobName and JobParameters  	
 5) Observe the output.xml and output_db.xml inside the xml folder	
 [Note: xml folder and output.xml file can be deleted. Both will be created on execution]
 
Notes:

	Heart of Spring Batch is a job. 
	Job is template which tells how batch processing has to be performed.
	Job has following:
		Instances(logical run of a job is called job instance)
		JobExecution(attempt to run a job )
		ExecutionContext
		Parameters
	Steps 1 or more, a job can have one more steps)
		They define a phase of processing (reading, processing, writing )
		spring-batch-reference-model.png
	StepExecution

Refer => https://docs.spring.io/spring-batch/docs/4.3.4/reference/html/step.html#controllingStepFlow	
	
 
